-- 41. CLEARSCOPE
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d41$Clearscope$d41$,
  url         = $d41$https://clearscope.io$d41$,
  domain      = $d41$clearscope.io$d41$,
  badge       = $d41$paid$d41$,
  best_for    = $d41$SEO content optimization, content inventory, LLM visibility tracking$d41$,
  description = $d41$Clearscope 2.0 rebranded as a full discoverability platform with AI-assisted drafting, Content Inventory Monitoring with Striking Distance and Content Decay views, and LLM tracking. New Essentials plan at $129/mo.$d41$,
  description_long = $dl41$Clearscope is an SEO content optimization platform that underwent a major rebrand with version 2.0, repositioning itself from a keyword-grading tool to a full discoverability platform. The update introduces a broader set of content lifecycle features designed to cover not just new content creation but ongoing inventory management and AI search visibility.

Draft with AI is one of the headline additions in Clearscope 2.0. It provides SEO-optimized content creation directly inside the platform and is available on all plans — not restricted to higher tiers. The feature previously called Reports has been renamed Drafts, aligning the nomenclature with the new AI-assisted writing workflow.

Content Inventory Monitoring adds two analytical views for managing existing content. Striking Distance surfaces pages that rank between positions 8 and 20 for target keywords — pages that are close to ranking on the first page and could be pushed up with targeted optimization. Content Decay identifies pages whose traffic or rankings have declined over a defined period, flagging them for refresh or consolidation before the decline compounds.

LLM tracking is a new capability that monitors how content appears in responses generated by large language models including ChatGPT, Perplexity, and similar AI search engines. This reflects the growing importance of AI search visibility alongside traditional Google rankings. Local SEO Targeting adds location-specific optimization for businesses targeting geographic search queries.

Pricing was restructured with the introduction of a new Essentials plan at $129 per month. Clearscope has eliminated feature gating on this tier — all features are available across plans, with the distinction being scale and usage limits rather than capability restrictions.

Clearscope is best for SEO content teams and agencies that need to optimize both new and existing content, monitor AI search visibility, and manage large content inventories with decay and striking-distance analysis.$dl41$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Draft with AI on all plans — SEO-optimized content creation without plan restrictions',
    'Striking Distance view identifies near-first-page content for targeted quick wins',
    'Content Decay monitoring flags declining pages before traffic loss compounds',
    'LLM tracking adds AI search visibility alongside traditional Google ranking data',
    'New Essentials plan at $129/mo with no feature gating — full access from entry tier'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Paid-only starting at $129/mo — no free trial or meaningful free tier',
    'LLM tracking is a newer feature — coverage and accuracy across AI engines still maturing',
    'Feature set focused on SEO teams — less useful for general content writers without SEO context',
    'Higher-tier plans required for large-scale inventory monitoring at enterprise content volume'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d41$clearscope$d41$ AND lang = $d41$en$d41$;

-- ============================================================
-- 42. PERPLEXITY
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d42$Perplexity$d42$,
  url         = $d42$https://perplexity.ai$d42$,
  domain      = $d42$perplexity.ai$d42$,
  badge       = $d42$freemium$d42$,
  best_for    = $d42$AI search, deep research, agentic computer control, finance and study tools$d42$,
  description = $d42$Perplexity Deep Research now runs on Claude Opus 4.6. Personal Computer for Mac adds agentic control features for all users. Kimi K2.5 added to inference stack. Microsoft Teams integration and finance and study tools launched.$d42$,
  description_long = $dl42$Perplexity is an AI-powered search and research platform that answers queries with cited sources rather than a list of links. It is used for real-time research, fact-checking, competitive analysis, and academic study by individuals, researchers, and business teams. Perplexity's model stack is multi-provider, drawing on models from Anthropic, OpenAI, Mistral, and others.

Deep Research, Perplexity's long-form research capability, has been upgraded to run on Claude Opus 4.6, reflecting improved benchmark performance for complex multi-step research tasks. Deep Research conducts autonomous web searches, synthesizes findings across multiple sources, and produces structured reports with inline citations — suitable for tasks that would otherwise require hours of manual research.

Personal Computer for Mac is a native Mac application that extends Perplexity beyond search into agentic computer control. It can interact with on-screen content, automate desktop tasks, and respond to natural language instructions that require operating the computer itself. The feature is available to all users — not restricted to Pro subscribers. Perplexity also became available as a Microsoft Teams application, enabling the same computer-control agent capability within the Teams enterprise environment.

Kimi K2.5, the open-source model from Moonshot AI, has been added to Perplexity's inference stack as a selectable model option. This expands the model choices available to users running queries on the platform and introduces a capable open-source alternative to the closed models already offered.

Finance tools include an ETF holdings tab that displays portfolio composition data directly in Perplexity search results, useful for investors and analysts. Study tools on the iOS app can generate quizzes and flashcards from any content — articles, documents, or pages — for spaced-repetition learning.

Perplexity is free for standard use. Pro plan is $20 per month and adds Deep Research, model selection including Claude Opus 4.6, and higher usage limits. Perplexity is best for researchers, students, and professionals who need cited, real-time answers and want AI search with agentic capabilities beyond a standard chat interface.$dl42$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Deep Research on Claude Opus 4.6 — cited multi-step research reports for complex queries',
    'Personal Computer for Mac: agentic desktop control available to all users, not Pro-only',
    'Kimi K2.5 open-source model added to inference stack alongside Claude, GPT-4o, and others',
    'ETF holdings tab and iOS quiz/flashcard generation — practical finance and study integrations',
    'Microsoft Teams app brings Perplexity Computer into enterprise environments'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Deep Research and model selection require Pro plan at $20/mo',
    'Agentic computer control on Mac is new — reliability on complex multi-step tasks varies',
    'Perplexity search can surface inaccurate citations — source verification remains necessary',
    'Finance data (ETF holdings) is informational and may lag real-time market data sources'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d42$perplexity$d42$ AND lang = $d42$en$d42$;

-- ============================================================
-- 43. MICROSOFT COPILOT
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d43$Microsoft Copilot$d43$,
  url         = $d43$https://copilot.microsoft.com$d43$,
  domain      = $d43$copilot.microsoft.com$d43$,
  badge       = $d43$freemium$d43$,
  best_for    = $d43$AI assistant, autonomous task delegation, M365 integration, Windows AI$d43$,
  description = $d43$Copilot Cowork launches agentic task delegation on iOS/Android. Microsoft 365 E7 + Agent 365 bundles Copilot enterprise-wide. Windows 11 May 2026 update adds taskbar AI agent monitoring and File Explorer enhancements.$d43$,
  description_long = $dl43$Microsoft Copilot is Microsoft's AI assistant platform integrated across Windows, Microsoft 365, mobile, and web. It is powered by models from OpenAI and Microsoft Research, and serves as the primary AI interface across the Microsoft ecosystem — from the Windows taskbar to Outlook, Teams, Word, Excel, and enterprise automation through the Power Platform.

Copilot Cowork, part of the Frontier program, introduces autonomous agentic task delegation. Available on iOS and Android, it allows users to assign real tasks — scheduling, research, drafting, web-based actions — and have Copilot execute them in the background without continuous user supervision. This moves Copilot from a chat assistant that responds to queries toward a delegated agent that completes multi-step tasks independently.

Microsoft 365 E7 is a new enterprise licensing tier that bundles Microsoft 365 E5, Copilot, and Agent 365 into a single plan. Agent 365 is the enterprise agent layer that enables organizations to build, deploy, and govern AI agents across their Microsoft environments. This consolidation simplifies procurement for large enterprises that previously needed separate SKUs for M365, Copilot, and automation capabilities.

Copilot Insights in Outlook Classic brings AI-generated email intelligence into the traditional Outlook desktop client. Users can ask Copilot about selected email text, receive AI-generated summaries of thread history, and surface action items without switching to the Outlook new app or the web version.

The Windows 11 May 2026 update embedded Copilot more deeply into the operating system. An AI agent monitoring indicator appears in the taskbar when Copilot is actively executing a background task, providing status visibility. File Explorer received AI-enhanced search and file management suggestions. Xbox mode adds a gaming-optimized interface layer accessible directly through Windows.

Microsoft Copilot is free with a Microsoft account at basic capability. Microsoft 365 Personal and Family plans include Copilot from $6 per user per month. Enterprise plans vary. Copilot is best for organizations already in the Microsoft ecosystem who want unified AI assistance, autonomous task agents, and deep integration with M365 applications.$dl43$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Copilot Cowork: autonomous task delegation on iOS/Android — true background agent execution',
    'M365 E7 bundles Copilot + Agent 365 with M365 E5 — simplified enterprise procurement',
    'Copilot Insights in Outlook Classic — AI email intelligence without switching to new app',
    'Windows 11 integration: taskbar agent monitoring and File Explorer AI enhancements',
    'Free tier available with a Microsoft account — lowest entry barrier of any major AI assistant'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Copilot Cowork (Frontier program) is still in early access — not broadly available yet',
    'Full enterprise capabilities require M365 E7 or separate Copilot licensing at significant cost',
    'Quality varies significantly across M365 apps — more polished in Teams and Word than Excel',
    'Agentic features on mobile are new — reliability and scope of supported tasks still limited'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d43$microsoft-copilot$d43$ AND lang = $d43$en$d43$;

-- ============================================================
-- 44. STABLE DIFFUSION
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d44$Stable Diffusion$d44$,
  url         = $d44$https://stability.ai$d44$,
  domain      = $d44$stability.ai$d44$,
  badge       = $d44$free$d44$,
  best_for    = $d44$Open-source image generation, local inference, video AI, audio generation$d44$,
  description = $d44$Stability AI cleared its debt and signed an EA partnership in February 2026. SD3.5 is optimized for NVIDIA TensorRT/FP8 and AMD ONNX. SV4D 2.0 and Stable Audio Open Small launched with Arm partnership.$d44$,
  description_long = $dl44$Stable Diffusion is Stability AI's open-source image generation model series, widely used for local inference, fine-tuning, and commercial deployment. Unlike closed-source models, Stable Diffusion weights are publicly released and can be run on consumer hardware, making it the foundation of a large ecosystem of third-party tools, community fine-tunes, and commercial applications built on top of the base models.

Stability AI underwent a significant corporate recovery in early 2026. The company's debt was fully erased, resolving the financial instability that had threatened operations through 2024 and 2025. A strategic partnership with Electronic Arts (EA) was signed in February 2026, providing both capital and a high-profile commercial deployment context for Stability AI's models. James Cameron joined as an advisor, adding industry credibility to the company's video generation push.

SD3.5 performance has been improved through optimizations for NVIDIA TensorRT with FP8 quantization. This combination delivers faster inference speeds and significantly lower VRAM requirements on RTX-series GPUs, making SD3.5 more practical on mid-range consumer hardware than earlier large models. AMD support expanded through ONNX-optimized model variants designed for Radeon GPUs and Ryzen AI accelerators, broadening the addressable hardware base beyond NVIDIA.

SV4D 2.0 (Stable Video 4D 2.0) is a new video generation model release focused on higher-quality outputs for real-world scenes — improving coherence, motion quality, and subject consistency compared to the original SV4D release. Stable Audio Open Small, a compact audio generation model, was open-sourced in partnership with Arm and is optimized for efficient inference on Arm-based hardware.

All Stable Diffusion models remain free and open-source. The Stability AI platform offers a freemium API for hosted inference without local setup. Stable Diffusion is best for developers, researchers, and creative professionals who need open-source image and video generation they can run locally, fine-tune, or deploy commercially without per-image fees.$dl44$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Fully open-source — weights freely available for local use, fine-tuning, and commercial deployment',
    'SD3.5 optimized for NVIDIA TensorRT/FP8: faster inference and lower VRAM on RTX GPUs',
    'AMD ONNX-optimized variants for Radeon and Ryzen AI — not NVIDIA-exclusive',
    'SV4D 2.0 delivers higher-quality real-world video output over original SV4D',
    'Stable Audio Open Small open-sourced with Arm — audio generation available on edge hardware'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Local setup requires technical knowledge — not suitable for non-technical users',
    'Best results on SD3.5 still require a capable GPU; CPU-only inference is slow',
    'Open-source ecosystem is fragmented — many forks, versions, and UIs with inconsistent quality',
    'Stability AI corporate instability history — partnership sustainability remains to be proven'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d44$stable-diffusion$d44$ AND lang = $d44$en$d44$;

-- ============================================================
-- 45. CAPCUT
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d45$CapCut$d45$,
  url         = $d45$https://capcut.com$d45$,
  domain      = $d45$capcut.com$d45$,
  badge       = $d45$freemium$d45$,
  best_for    = $d45$AI video editing, auto-edit, story generation, 2K/4K export$d45$,
  description = $d45$CapCut returned to the US in January 2026 via TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC with Oracle/Silver Lake/MGX ownership. AI Auto-Edit, AI Story Maker with Google Veo 3 integration, and 2K/4K export launched in 2026.$d45$,
  description_long = $dl45$CapCut is a consumer and creator video editing application originally developed by ByteDance. It is widely used for short-form video production, social content creation, and increasingly for AI-assisted editing workflows. CapCut gained a large user base through tight integration with TikTok's creative ecosystem.

CapCut's availability in the United States was restored on January 22, 2026 following a legal and ownership resolution. The app is now operated through TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC, a new corporate structure with Oracle, Silver Lake, and MGX holding majority ownership. This structure was established to satisfy US national security requirements regarding data handling. All US users were migrated to the new "CapCut US" app by March 2026, replacing the previous ByteDance-operated version.

AI Auto-Edit is a 2026 AI feature that analyzes uploaded footage using scene recognition and speech transcription, assigns quality scores to clips, and automatically assembles a cut based on pacing and content relevance. Users can review and override the auto-assembled edit, or use it as a starting point for manual refinement. This significantly reduces the time required to produce a first cut from raw footage.

AI Story Maker integrates Google Veo 3 for AI video generation directly inside CapCut. Users describe a scene or narrative in text, and Story Maker generates corresponding video segments using Veo 3, which can be combined with captured footage or published as standalone AI-generated content.

Export quality improved with the addition of 2K and 4K export options, raising the output ceiling for professional and semi-professional use cases. CapCut remains free for core editing features. The Pro plan is $9.99 per month and adds AI credits, cloud storage, premium templates, and higher export quality tiers.

CapCut is best for social content creators, short-form video producers, and individuals who need fast AI-assisted editing with minimal technical setup, and for creators who want access to Google Veo 3 video generation inside a consumer-friendly editing environment.$dl45$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'AI Auto-Edit: scene recognition, speech transcription, and quality scoring automate first cuts',
    'AI Story Maker with Google Veo 3 integration — AI video generation inside the editing app',
    '2K and 4K export now available — higher output quality for semi-professional use',
    'Free tier covers core editing features — accessible without a subscription',
    'US legal status resolved — stable operation via TikTok USDS JV with Oracle/Silver Lake/MGX'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'US corporate structure is new — long-term data governance and ownership stability unproven',
    'AI Auto-Edit requires review — automated cuts often need manual adjustment for quality results',
    'AI credits for Story Maker and AI features consumed quickly on the free tier',
    'Pro at $9.99/mo is competitive but 2K/4K and full AI access require the paid plan'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d45$capcut$d45$ AND lang = $d45$en$d45$;
