-- 48. LEONARDO AI
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d48$Leonardo AI$d48$,
  url         = $d48$https://leonardo.ai$d48$,
  domain      = $d48$leonardo.ai$d48$,
  badge       = $d48$freemium$d48$,
  best_for    = $d48$AI image generation, sketch-to-image, image-to-video, enterprise API$d48$,
  description = $d48$Leonardo AI launched the Creative Engine API for enterprise replication, rebranded as "Yours to Create," and added Motion 2.0 with improved lip sync. Real-time sketch-to-image with sub-second updates is best-in-class as of May 2026.$d48$,
  description_long = $dl48$Leonardo AI is an AI image and video generation platform used by game developers, concept artists, marketers, and creative studios. It offers a web-based interface alongside a robust API, combining proprietary model pipelines with third-party model integrations. The platform is built for high-volume creative production and professional asset generation workflows.

The Creative Engine API, launched April 14, 2026, is an enterprise-grade API that enables code extraction and replication of Leonardo's generation pipelines. Enterprises can use it to embed Leonardo's image and video generation capabilities into proprietary tools, internal platforms, and production workflows without exposing end users to the Leonardo interface directly.

Leonardo underwent a full rebrand in April 2026, adopting the identity "Yours to Create" developed by agency Koto. The rebrand accompanied the release of the new Alchemy v4 pipeline and the Phoenix architecture — updated generation models that improve quality on photorealistic and stylized outputs and reduce artifact rates on complex compositions.

Third-party model integrations expanded significantly: Veo 3, Sora 2, Kling, and Seedance are now accessible directly through Leonardo's interface and API, allowing users to run multiple leading video generation models from a single platform without separate subscriptions.

Motion 2.0, the platform's image-to-video system, received updates improving motion coherence across longer clips, enabling longer output durations, and adding improved lip sync for talking-head and character animation use cases. Sketch-to-image reached sub-second real-time update speeds, making it the fastest sketch-to-image implementation available as of May 2026.

Leonardo AI is best for creative professionals, game developers, and enterprise teams who need high-volume image and video generation with access to multiple leading models from a single API and interface.$dl48$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Creative Engine API: enterprise code extraction and replication of generation pipelines',
    'Alchemy v4 and Phoenix architecture reduce artifacts on complex photorealistic outputs',
    'Integrates Veo 3, Sora 2, Kling, and Seedance — multiple top models in one platform',
    'Sketch-to-image with sub-second real-time updates — best-in-class speed as of May 2026',
    'Motion 2.0: better motion coherence, longer clips, and improved lip sync for video'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Enterprise Creative Engine API pricing not publicly listed — requires sales contact',
    'Multiple model integrations make the platform complex to navigate for new users',
    'Credit consumption varies by model — Veo 3 and Sora 2 are significantly more expensive per generation',
    'Free tier has limited daily token allocation — insufficient for professional volume use'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d48$leonardo-ai$d48$ AND lang = $d48$en$d48$;

-- ============================================================
-- 49. COMFYUI
-- ============================================================
UPDATE tools SET
  name        = $d49$ComfyUI$d49$,
  url         = $d49$https://comfyui.org$d49$,
  domain      = $d49$comfyui.org$d49$,
  badge       = $d49$free$d49$,
  best_for    = $d49$open-source AI image generation, node workflows, local GPU, 4K video$d49$,
  description = $d49$ComfyUI added an App View for beginners alongside the node editor, NVFP4 quantization for 2.5x speed on RTX 50 Series, AMD ROCm support, and Veo 3/Kling 3.0 nodes. Free and open-source.$d49$,
  description_long = $dl49$ComfyUI is a free, open-source node-based interface for running AI image and video generation models locally. Users build workflows by connecting nodes — each node performs one operation such as loading a model, applying a sampler, or encoding a prompt — giving precise control over every step of the generation process. It is the primary interface for users who run Stable Diffusion and other open-weight models on their own hardware.

App View, a major UX addition, provides a simplified interface that hides the node graph and presents a clean form-based UI for users who do not need to modify the underlying workflow. Node View remains fully available for advanced users. This dual-mode approach makes ComfyUI accessible to beginners without removing any capability from experienced users.

NVFP4 quantization, introduced for NVIDIA RTX 50 Series GPUs, enables generation to run 2.5 times faster while reducing VRAM consumption by approximately 60%. This means users with RTX 50 Series cards can run larger models that previously required more expensive hardware, or run existing models at substantially higher speeds.

Official AMD ROCm support landed for the Windows Desktop app, making ComfyUI fully supported on AMD GPUs on Windows for the first time without requiring manual workarounds. New nodes for Veo 3, Veo 3 Lite, and Kling 3.0 were added, along with 4K output support for ByteDance, Veo, and Kling video generation pipelines. RTX Video Super Resolution enables real-time 4K upscaling of generated video on supported NVIDIA hardware.

Python 3.13 compatibility was added, keeping ComfyUI current with the latest Python release and ensuring compatibility with newer packages in the Python ecosystem.

ComfyUI is best for advanced users, researchers, and developers who want full control over AI image and video generation workflows, run models locally on their own hardware, and need support for the latest open-weight and third-party models.$dl49$,
  pros = ARRAY[
    'Completely free and open-source — no subscription, no credit limits, no vendor dependency',
    'App View: beginner-friendly form UI without removing the full node graph for advanced users',
    'NVFP4 quantization: 2.5x faster generation and 60% less VRAM on RTX 50 Series GPUs',
    'Official AMD ROCm support on Windows — no manual workarounds required',
    'Veo 3, Kling 3.0 nodes and 4K video support via ByteDance/Veo/Kling pipelines'
  ],
  cons = ARRAY[
    'Node-based interface has a steep learning curve for users new to workflow-based generation',
    'Requires local GPU hardware — not suitable for users without a capable graphics card',
    'Community-maintained custom nodes vary in quality and may conflict with each other',
    'No cloud option — all computation is local; high-end hardware needed for large models'
  ]
WHERE slug = $d49$comfyui$d49$ AND lang = $d49$en$d49$;

